verses.text:
All hail the pow’r of Jesus’ name! Let angels prostrate fall! (2X)
Bring forth the royal diadem,
And crown Him Lord, of all;

Ye chosen seed of Isreal’s race, Ye ransomed from the fall, (2X)
Hail Him who saves you by His grace,
And crown, Him Lord of all;

Let ev‘ry kindred, ev‘ry tribe, On this terrestrail ball, (2X)
To Him all majesty ascribe,
And crown Him, Lord of all;

O that with yonder sacred through We at His feet may fall! (2X)
We’ll join the everlasting song,
And praise Him, Lord of all;

Perfect submission, all is at rest; I in my Savior am happy and blest;
Watching and waiting, looking above,
Filled with His goodness, lost in His love.

O verdant fields! O shining shore!
The Lamb of God spreads wide the door;
Ah, golden city surely I, shall see thy glories “by and by.”

Jesus loves me! this I know,
For the Bible tells me so;
Little ones to Him belong; They are weak but He is strong.

Yes, Jesus loves me;
Yes, Jesus loves me;
Yes, Jesus loves me;
The Bible tells me so.

My Jesus, I love Thee, I know Thou art mine;
For Thee all the follies of sin I resign;
My gracious Redeemer, my Savior art Thou:
If ever I loved Thee, my Jesus, ‘tis now.

Draw me nearer, near-er, bless-ed Lord,
To the cross where Thou hast died;
Draw me near-er, nearer, blessed Lord, To Thy precious, bleed-ing side.

Lord, lift me up and let me stand, By faith, on heaven’s tableland,
A higher, plane that I have found;
Lord plant my feet on higher ground.

I need Thee ev‘ry hour, Most gracious Lord;
No tendor voice like Thine,
Can peace afford.

I need Thee ev‘ry hour: Stay Thou near by;
Temp-ta-taions lose their pow’r,
When Thou art nigh.

I need Thee ev‘ry hour, In joy or pain;
Come quick-ly and abide,
Or life is vain.

I need Thee ev‘ry hour, Most Holy One;
O make me Thine indeed,
Thou blessed Son!

Plen-teous grace with Thee is found, Grace to cover all my sin;
Let the healing stream abound;
Make and keep me pure within.
Thou of life the fountain art,
Freely let me take of Thee;
Spring Thou up with-in my heart, Rise to all eternity.

Love divine, all love excelling, Joy of heav’n earth, come down! Fix in us Thy humble dwell-ing, All Thy faithfull mer-cies crown;
Jesus, Thuo art all compassion,
Pure, un-bound-ed love Thou art;
Visit us with Thy salvation, Enter ev‘ry trem-bling heart!

Breathe, O breathe Thy loving Spirit Into ev‘ry trou-ble breast;
Let us all in Thee inherit;
Let us find the prom-ised rest;
Take away the love of sinning, Take our load of guilt aaway;
End the word of Thy beginning, Bring us to eternal day.

Come, almighty to deliver, Let us all Thy life receive;
Sud-denly return, and never more Thy temples leave;
Thee we would be always bless-ing, Serve Thee as Thy hosts above,
Pray, and praise Thee, with-out ceasing, Glory in Thy per-fect love.

There is a name I love to hear, I love to sing its worth;
It sounds like music in mine ear,
The sweetest name on earth.

Jesus knows all about our stug-gles;
He will guide till the day is done; There’s not a friend like the lowly Jesus,
No, not one! No, not one!
